  "body": "The spec defines some steps to take when `<embed>`'s `src` attribute changes: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/iframe-embed-object.html#attr-embed-src\r\n\r\nBut it doesn't say what needs to be done with any previously-loaded plugin or nested browsing context.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, `<object>` runs a set of steps to determine the handler when `data`, etc changes, but doesn't state what should be done with any previously-loaded embedded content.\r\n\r\nIn particular:\r\n- if the embedded content is a nested browsing context, should it receive `unload` events?\r\n- what about `beforeunload` events? This could be problematic, since plugin loads are synchronous in Chrome (if you try to touch an attribute on the element before it's done, Chrome will synchronously complete plugin loading)",
